From: UN1CA <unica@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Stage dm3q wide-pair Portrait baseline at1x to2x

Keep failed trial0006 disabled. Pin rear Portrait to camera23 and the legacy
DualBokehPhotoMaker, with1..2 bounds matching the inspected provider metadata.
Start rear sessions at1x; ignore remembered3x values. Omit both tele shortcuts.
Clamp live Portrait camera23 requests to1000..2000 before deriving Samsung
scaler.zoomRatio and the center crop from that same value. Preserve existing
register counts and the front Portrait initialization value. No vendor library,
calibration or native crop-command adaptation. Runtime baseline validation is
required; this is not a validated1..2x port and does not enable3x.

--- a/smali_classes2/te/l0.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/te/l0.smali
@@ -1450,6 +1450,24 @@
 .method public static g(Ll9/j0;IIZ)Ll9/x;
     .locals 3

+    if-nez p1, :cond_wide_baseline_original
+
+    sget-object v0, Ll9/j0;->SHOOTING_MODE_PORTRAIT:Ll9/j0;
+
+    if-ne p0, v0, :cond_wide_baseline_original
+
+    invoke-static {}, Lcom/rezoss/camera/PortraitWideBaseline;->enabled()Z
+
+    move-result v0
+
+    if-eqz v0, :cond_wide_baseline_original
+
+    sget-object v0, Ll9/x;->BACK_NORMAL_DUAL_PORTRAIT:Ll9/x;
+
+    return-object v0
+
+    :cond_wide_baseline_original
+
     if-eqz p1, :cond_4

     const/4 p2, 0x1
